{title: 453 - We Have Heard}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #453 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 453}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G/D]We have heard from the bright, the holy, land;
[G]We have heard, and our hearts [C]are [G]glad;
[G]For we [D7]were a [G]lonely pilgrim band,
[G]And weary, and worn, and sad.
[G]They tell us the saints have a dwelling there-
[C]No longer [G/D]are homeless [D7]ones;
[G]And we know that the goodly [D]land is [D7]fair,
[D7]Where life's pure river runs.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G/D]They say green fields are waving there,
[G]That never a blight [C]shall [G]know;
[G]And the [D7]deserts [G]wild are blooming fair,
[G]And the roses of Sharon grow.
[G]There are lovely birds in the bowers green,
[C]Their songs [G/D]are blithe [D7]and [G]sweet;
[G]And their warblings, gushing [D]ever [D7]new,
[D7]The angels' harpings greet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G/D]We have heard of the palms, the robes, the crowns,
[G]And the silvery band [C]in [G]white;
[G]Of the [D7]city [G]fair, with pearly gates,
[G]All radiant with light.
[G]We have heard of the angels there, and saints,
[C]With their [G/D]harps of gold, [D7]how they [G]sing;
[G]Of the mount with the fruitful [D]tree of [D7]life,
[D7]Of the leaves that healing bring.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G/D]The King of that country, He is fair,
[G]He's the joy and light of [C]the [G]place;
[G]In His [D7]beauty [G]we shall behold Him there,
[G]And bask in His smiling face,
[G]We'll be there, we'll be there in a little while,
[C]We'll join [G/D]the pure and [D7]the [G]blest;
[G]We'll have the palm, the [D]robe, the [D7]crown,
[D7]And forever be at rest.
{end_of_verse}
